        "why": "The whole Ulam east face (X -2500, Y +-2500, Z 925..6075) is ONE union mesh still carrying the FinishPilot procedural stone (census: 1 slot, native-scale-inventory-20260908T133142). Its base colour is the canonical 'blue' pale stone [0.776,0.680,0.497] -> luma 0.69 linear vs 0.30 for MI_PBR_LimestoneAshlar: +1.2 stops brighter than the side walls under the same 35 deg sun, so it sits at sRGB 232 (p95) while the meter sits on the shaded court. Re-pointing the component to the V3 limestone instance (map-level override, like the PBR pass) is the material fix; no shared material is edited."
